WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:53.918
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:54.188 --> 00:55.813
Eat your meal and take your medicine.

3
01:20.146 --> 01:21.563
I love the smell of rain.

4
01:23.521 --> 01:24.646
Once it stops,

5
01:25.605 --> 01:26.896
want to go for a walk?

6
01:34.896 --> 01:37.146
Finish your meal and take your medicine first.

7
03:13.230 --> 03:14.063
Inspector.

8
03:15.521 --> 03:18.063
The forensics team will be here soon.

9
03:21.271 --> 03:23.021
Did anyone photograph the scene yet?

10
03:24.105 --> 03:25.313
Yes, we did.

11
03:27.688 --> 03:28.605
Phii Pong.

12
03:29.188 --> 03:32.730
Narong's definitely the Phii Pong.

13
03:32.813 --> 03:34.896
If they hadn't let him out,

14
03:34.980 --> 03:37.230
Shaman Sak wouldn't have died.

15
03:42.771 --> 03:43.938
It wanted revenge.

16
03:44.021 --> 03:47.313
Shaman Sak knew what he was.

17
03:47.396 --> 03:49.063
He knew he was a Phii Pong.

18
04:00.855 --> 04:02.605
Don't worry.

19
04:03.355 --> 04:05.771
Everything will work itself out.

20
05:19.480 --> 05:24.313
DELUSION

21
05:36.188 --> 05:37.230
Your investigation

22
05:38.063 --> 05:39.521
into Mued's murder was solid.

23
05:41.896 --> 05:43.563
Too bad the suspect died first.

24
05:44.355 --> 05:47.063
Yes, sir. But I think there's another perpetrator

25
05:47.938 --> 05:49.980
who knows the details of the bodies very well.

26
05:51.938 --> 05:53.105
Everyone around here

27
05:53.188 --> 05:54.438
already knows them.

28
05:55.480 --> 05:57.771
Since the Phii Pong case all those years ago.

29
06:00.646 --> 06:03.271
What about the cases from the other provinces?

30
06:03.855 --> 06:05.271
What are we doing about those?

31
06:09.938 --> 06:11.813
We'll be closing one case,

32
06:12.646 --> 06:13.771
but opening a new one.

33
06:14.896 --> 06:18.563
Honestly, I'd rather not drag cases from other provinces into this.

34
06:19.188 --> 06:22.021
Because the evidence archives aren't linked anyway.

35
06:23.188 --> 06:25.646
Just figuring out who killed Sak

36
06:26.730 --> 06:28.271
is already enough of a headache.

37
06:28.355 --> 06:30.480
Please give me a little more time, sir.

38
06:32.396 --> 06:33.646
I can do that.

39
06:34.396 --> 06:36.188
But I don't want this to become a big deal

40
06:36.813 --> 06:38.563
that attracts the media.

41
06:39.188 --> 06:42.313
The more attention it gets, the harder it'll be to get the job done.

42
06:49.021 --> 06:50.646
Just be careful, all right?

43
06:51.980 --> 06:52.938
Yes, sir.

44
07:14.063 --> 07:15.688
They can't release the body yet.

45
07:17.146 --> 07:18.355
The examiner isn't done.

46
07:19.771 --> 07:20.646
So now what?

47
07:23.771 --> 07:24.980
I'm tired of waiting.

48
07:25.771 --> 07:27.188
Let's just hold the funeral.

49
07:28.355 --> 07:29.980
Waiting won't change anything.

50
07:30.480 --> 07:33.021
I'm his only relative anyway.

51
07:39.980 --> 07:41.480
How long do you want it to be?

52
07:44.355 --> 07:47.271
Three days is enough. It's a waste of money.

53
07:50.355 --> 07:52.271
Dad didn't go anywhere that night, did he?

54
07:54.438 --> 07:55.271
Why?

55
07:56.730 --> 07:58.480
You think your father's the killer?

56
07:59.563 --> 08:01.396
I'm just asking.

57
08:01.480 --> 08:02.605
Can we go now?

58
08:03.480 --> 08:04.521
I need to go to the temple

59
08:04.605 --> 08:06.396
and be done with the funeral arrangements.

60
08:22.271 --> 08:24.063
-Yes? -Mrs. Wanrudee.

61
08:24.146 --> 08:26.313
It's Supattra, Mr. Yote's lawyer.

62
08:26.396 --> 08:27.230
Yes.

63
08:27.771 --> 08:29.771
I'm calling to check on the mediation date.

64
08:31.146 --> 08:33.313
Your lawyer still hasn't contacted us.

65
08:36.730 --> 08:38.730
I've been really busy lately.

66
08:38.813 --> 08:40.980
I'll get back to you when I'm free.

67
08:41.063 --> 08:41.896
Please hurry.

68
08:42.480 --> 08:44.480
I'd rather this doesn't end up in court.

69
08:45.605 --> 08:47.688
What happened between your father and Aim

70
08:48.480 --> 08:50.188
doesn't need to be brought up.

71
09:11.646 --> 09:12.480
Inspector.

72
09:13.146 --> 09:14.146
Have a look at this.

73
09:18.021 --> 09:21.230
Saeng's son filmed it from next door.

74
09:21.313 --> 09:23.480
He woke up because he heard Narong shouting.

75
09:24.980 --> 09:29.438
There are ghosts in the forest. You can't go in.

76
09:29.521 --> 09:32.146
-Where is he now? -He's with the duty officer.

77
09:33.230 --> 09:35.146
Sergeant, make a copy of this clip for me.

78
09:35.813 --> 09:36.938
Already done, sir.

79
09:37.021 --> 09:37.855
Thank you.

80
10:10.355 --> 10:13.188
ANUPONG'S PHOTO

81
10:13.271 --> 10:15.396
PACHARA JUNSAYPUN PORNCHAI JAMROON

82
10:15.480 --> 10:17.605
SAK SONGSIPHAN

83
10:55.730 --> 10:56.855
Hello, ma'am.

84
11:11.021 --> 11:12.396
Water, sir.

85
11:14.980 --> 11:16.480
My condolences.

86
11:17.105 --> 11:18.855
The police are doing everything they can.

87
11:19.563 --> 11:21.396
Whoever killed your brother

88
11:21.480 --> 11:22.980
will be caught.

89
11:25.355 --> 11:27.605
Here's my donation.

90
11:32.480 --> 11:36.896
He lived all by himself. That place is huge.

91
11:37.730 --> 11:40.396
He didn't have any relatives except you, did he?

92
11:41.271 --> 11:42.313
No.

93
11:42.396 --> 11:45.646
So I guess the land goes to you.

94
11:47.855 --> 11:49.355
A blessing in disguise, isn't it?

95
11:51.105 --> 11:53.271
I don't know anything about that, sir.

96
11:54.646 --> 11:56.438
The reason I came

97
11:56.521 --> 11:59.688
is to leave the land mortgage agreement with you.

98
12:04.480 --> 12:08.063
He mortgaged his land to me for over 200,000.

99
12:09.230 --> 12:12.938
He barely paid anything back. The interest is higher than the principal.

100
12:14.355 --> 12:17.605
I'll round it down for you, leaving it at 350,000.

101
12:17.688 --> 12:21.646
Pay me back, and I'll return the land to you.

102
12:22.605 --> 12:23.855
I understand.

103
12:24.688 --> 12:28.355
You never even got to use the money, and now you're stuck with the debt.

104
12:28.438 --> 12:31.105
But we still have to follow the law, ma'am.

105
12:32.396 --> 12:34.021
We're not strangers.

106
12:34.105 --> 12:37.438
I'd rather this didn't end up in court.

107
12:45.730 --> 12:48.063
Inspector.

108
12:49.646 --> 12:50.480
He's not here.

109
12:53.271 --> 12:54.105
Sergeant.

110
12:54.188 --> 12:55.021
Oh, you're here.

111
12:56.146 --> 12:59.438
If we rule out the missing teeth, could the killer still be the same person?

112
13:06.146 --> 13:07.688
From the Land Office.

113
13:43.313 --> 13:44.771
I only took a quick look, Sergeant,

114
13:46.188 --> 13:47.480
but I think the shack

115
13:48.230 --> 13:50.271
is on Narong's property.

116
13:50.938 --> 13:55.188
71 YEARS OLD, MEMORY IMPAIRMENT, SUSPECT

117
13:59.563 --> 14:00.688
Where are you going?

118
14:01.688 --> 14:03.813
To the temple. I'm going to make merit.

119
14:05.938 --> 14:07.730
Why are you wearing black?

120
14:08.480 --> 14:10.896
People don't wear black to make merit.

121
14:12.521 --> 14:15.105
I'll bring you something to eat later.

122
14:31.396 --> 14:35.105
There are ghosts in the forest. You can't go in.

123
14:37.188 --> 14:38.396
When he wakes up to pee,

124
14:39.063 --> 14:40.396
he asks to walk around.

125
14:41.146 --> 14:43.480
I let him, only for about ten minutes.

126
14:43.563 --> 14:46.230
After that, I tie him up until morning.

127
14:47.146 --> 14:49.438
He lets you tie him up that easily, ma'am?

128
14:51.438 --> 14:52.980
Only when he's asleep,

129
14:53.063 --> 14:55.021
or when he's really groggy from the medication.

130
14:55.105 --> 14:56.563
Otherwise, he won't let us.

131
14:58.146 --> 14:58.980
I see.

132
15:01.730 --> 15:03.188
You're not lying to me, are you?

133
15:07.188 --> 15:09.313
If you are, I can't help your husband.

134
15:10.396 --> 15:11.438
Help with what?

135
15:11.521 --> 15:12.688
How is he involved in this?

136
15:15.146 --> 15:17.396
Did your brother have a fight with anyone?

137
15:17.480 --> 15:19.230
He died suddenly, just like Mued.

138
15:19.771 --> 15:22.313
If you think my husband did it, then go arrest him.

139
15:22.896 --> 15:24.730
Mom, come on.

140
15:27.730 --> 15:28.896
If you want to know more,

141
15:29.730 --> 15:31.521
ask him yourself. I'm leaving.

142
15:32.771 --> 15:33.605
It's all right.

143
15:35.563 --> 15:36.813
We'll let him get some rest.

144
15:37.855 --> 15:40.313
Please take good care of him during this time.

145
15:40.980 --> 15:42.813
Don't let him wander off and get into trouble.

146
15:43.771 --> 15:45.480
Sak's case is still open.

147
15:46.063 --> 15:48.480
People will start saying he's the Phii Pong again.

148
15:52.230 --> 15:54.730
Come on, Mom. Let's go inside. I'll take you to the temple.

149
15:57.313 --> 15:58.563
She's lying, Inspector.

150
15:59.230 --> 16:01.646
Her lips were trembling. Did you see that?

151
16:03.438 --> 16:06.480
LAWYER SUPATTRA: IF YOU CANNOT SCHEDULE THE MEDIATION,

152
16:06.563 --> 16:09.730
MR. YOTE WILL FILE FOR DIVORCE AND PRESS CHARGES AGAINST MR. NARONG.

153
16:19.938 --> 16:21.980
-Did you get a mosquito bite, kid? -Yes.

154
16:23.396 --> 16:25.355
Here.

155
16:26.771 --> 16:27.605
Come on.

156
16:29.438 --> 16:30.646
Why do you look so down?

157
16:31.230 --> 16:32.355
Is something wrong?

158
16:33.980 --> 16:34.813
I'm fine.

159
16:36.938 --> 16:38.813
Did you beat that boss yet?

160
16:40.980 --> 16:42.855
The one that attacks really fast.

161
16:43.480 --> 16:44.980
-I did. -Really?

162
16:45.980 --> 16:47.105
You didn't break the joystick, right?

163
16:47.188 --> 16:48.021
No.

164
16:54.480 --> 16:55.855
Do you miss me at all?

165
17:02.313 --> 17:03.230
Mom.

166
17:05.480 --> 17:07.938
I got accepted to a school in Bangkok.

167
17:08.521 --> 17:12.230
Dad said I'll be starting in the middle of the semester.

168
17:14.646 --> 17:15.480
Oh.

169
17:28.813 --> 17:31.938
Then I guess I'd better find a job in Bangkok soon.

170
17:33.938 --> 17:35.563
If we live apart,

171
17:36.438 --> 17:38.271
I'll miss you too much.

172
17:43.313 --> 17:47.605
Then I'll tell Dad to wait until you find a job

173
17:47.688 --> 17:48.521
before we move.

174
17:58.188 --> 17:59.605
Bangkok's a nice place.

175
18:01.105 --> 18:02.855
There are great schools

176
18:02.938 --> 18:04.438
and big malls.

177
18:05.063 --> 18:06.771
I think you're going to love it.

178
18:13.521 --> 18:15.855
Do you want to go get some ice cream?

179
18:17.521 --> 18:18.605
I'll bring you back.

180
18:20.105 --> 18:21.063
-Let's go. -Okay.

181
18:29.521 --> 18:30.355
Mom.

182
18:31.938 --> 18:32.771
Mom.

183
18:33.438 --> 18:35.855
We're not really getting ice cream, are we?

184
18:37.855 --> 18:40.771
If you're going to Grandpa's house, I'm not going with you.

185
18:49.063 --> 18:50.063
Why not?

186
18:54.313 --> 18:55.521
Because my family's poor?

187
18:56.813 --> 18:58.396
Did your grandpa do something to you?

188
18:59.105 --> 19:00.688
What did you tell Dad?

189
19:01.438 --> 19:02.896
Tell me too.

190
19:04.355 --> 19:05.688
I didn't tell him anything.

191
19:06.438 --> 19:07.396
Aim.

192
19:08.771 --> 19:10.188
Don't lie to me.

193
19:11.938 --> 19:13.355
Don't lie to me!

194
19:16.355 --> 19:17.230
Look at me.

195
19:18.313 --> 19:19.188
What did you say?

196
19:22.063 --> 19:24.146
Grandpa pushed me into the water.

197
19:24.230 --> 19:25.771
Out of nowhere.

198
19:26.355 --> 19:29.813
It was like he had gone crazy. He wasn't making any sense.

199
19:33.938 --> 19:34.938
Aim.

200
19:39.855 --> 19:44.563
Then why didn't you tell me or the police?

201
19:44.646 --> 19:48.438
I was afraid Dad would blame you.

202
20:02.188 --> 20:03.480
Don't cry.

203
20:03.563 --> 20:05.063
You didn't do anything wrong.

204
20:09.146 --> 20:10.271
I'm sorry, dear.

205
20:10.355 --> 20:11.646
I was too hasty.

206
20:16.230 --> 20:18.563
Go back to your dad now, okay?

207
20:18.646 --> 20:20.105
He must be worried about you.

208
20:22.438 --> 20:24.813
We'll see each other at your red belt test.

209
20:27.688 --> 20:28.688
See you, Son.

210
20:33.480 --> 20:34.730
See you later.

211
22:09.771 --> 22:12.480
BORN 14 MAY 1962 DIED 18 NOVEMBER 2026

212
22:20.646 --> 22:22.271
NEVER TO WAKE

213
22:22.355 --> 22:25.313
NEVER TO RETURN

214
22:42.188 --> 22:43.771
My donation.

215
22:43.855 --> 22:44.855
Thank you.

216
22:49.813 --> 22:51.230
Take your father home first.

217
22:51.313 --> 22:53.230
I'll take care of things here

218
22:53.313 --> 22:55.355
and have someone take me home.

219
22:56.771 --> 22:58.105
Go home first.

220
23:13.855 --> 23:15.105
Thank you for coming.

221
23:15.188 --> 23:17.271
It's fine.

222
23:17.355 --> 23:20.021
We live so close together. We're practically family.

223
23:22.313 --> 23:23.730
Narong's got good medicine.

224
23:24.355 --> 23:25.938
He's doing much better.

225
23:27.605 --> 23:29.146
He didn't kill Mued.

226
23:30.021 --> 23:31.396
Did the police tell you?

227
23:31.480 --> 23:32.605
Yeah, they did.

228
23:32.688 --> 23:36.105
Then stop sticking your nose into my family's business.

229
23:37.563 --> 23:39.980
Mind your own family instead.

230
24:14.855 --> 24:15.855
Trouble at home?

231
24:17.855 --> 24:18.980
You shouldn't be stressed.

232
24:19.980 --> 24:21.646
Your family's loaded. Don't you know?

233
24:21.730 --> 24:23.646
Just say what you want to say.

234
24:23.730 --> 24:24.688
I am saying it.

235
24:27.646 --> 24:29.438
Your family owns a lot of land.

236
24:33.396 --> 24:34.355
Sak's land

237
24:35.605 --> 24:36.480
is your family's.

238
24:37.896 --> 24:39.980
The land of the Phii Pong forest as well.

239
24:43.855 --> 24:46.521
Now, your father is ill and your uncle is gone.

240
24:47.605 --> 24:49.521
Your mother is the only one who knows.

241
24:56.938 --> 24:57.938
I'm telling you.

242
24:59.521 --> 25:01.271
If you've got evidence, arrest her.

243
25:04.021 --> 25:06.230
You're asking me, but I don't know that much.

244
25:08.063 --> 25:09.063
I'm the daughter…

245
25:10.646 --> 25:13.063
who's learning about my family from someone else.

246
25:18.521 --> 25:20.896
Do you think your brother knows about this land?

247
25:21.813 --> 25:23.188
No.

248
25:26.313 --> 25:27.563
Then that's all I needed.

249
25:30.313 --> 25:31.730
If I learn anything new,

250
25:32.855 --> 25:36.105
I'll ask you to give an official statement at the station.

251
25:38.271 --> 25:39.105
That's all.

252
26:00.063 --> 26:01.021
Walk quietly.

253
26:01.771 --> 26:03.146
You'll wake your father.

254
26:38.521 --> 26:41.021
-What are you looking for? -The land title deed.

255
26:41.980 --> 26:43.938
Or anything we can sell.

256
26:58.313 --> 26:59.146
Is this it?

257
26:59.230 --> 27:00.230
LAND TITLE DEED

258
27:12.855 --> 27:15.063
Why did you transfer Dad's land to Uncle Sak?

259
27:17.896 --> 27:20.146
You didn't want to leave it for your children?

260
27:21.646 --> 27:23.063
That's our business.

261
27:23.146 --> 27:24.355
Why do you care?

262
27:26.021 --> 27:27.355
When you do these things,

263
27:28.105 --> 27:29.938
have you ever thought of telling me?

264
27:31.063 --> 27:32.813
Were you planning to leave it all to Wat?

265
27:35.063 --> 27:37.480
You don't know anything. So don't say anything.

266
27:37.563 --> 27:38.396
Stay out of it.

267
27:39.063 --> 27:40.521
I don't want to get involved.

268
27:42.271 --> 27:43.980
But whenever something goes wrong,

269
27:45.313 --> 27:46.188
it always

270
27:47.730 --> 27:49.688
ends up falling on me.

271
27:50.521 --> 27:52.105
Go back to your own house.

272
27:53.063 --> 27:54.271
We'll manage on our own.

273
27:55.896 --> 27:57.855
Why do you hate me so much, Mom?

274
28:02.771 --> 28:05.813
Marrying that bastard

275
28:07.688 --> 28:11.521
was the only way to keep this poor family from falling apart.

276
28:12.980 --> 28:14.063
Have you ever thought

277
28:14.938 --> 28:16.063
about what

278
28:16.730 --> 28:18.313
I had to give up?

279
28:21.063 --> 28:23.896
I've done everything for this family.

280
28:25.980 --> 28:27.605
I've never even heard

281
28:29.105 --> 28:30.480
a single thank you.

282
28:33.188 --> 28:34.021
Me neither.

283
28:34.896 --> 28:37.980
No one's ever thanked me either.

284
28:47.021 --> 28:47.855
Thank you.

285
29:08.605 --> 29:11.438
If we set aside the cases from the other provinces for now,

286
29:11.521 --> 29:13.605
the people I suspect the most

287
29:13.688 --> 29:15.938
are Narong's entire family.

288
29:16.688 --> 29:18.980
The murder of Thongdee's son

289
29:19.063 --> 29:21.021
took place on the land owned by Narong's family,

290
29:21.813 --> 29:23.230
near the shack

291
29:23.313 --> 29:26.105
his family claimed they didn't know who owned.

292
29:26.188 --> 29:27.313
But in that same year,

293
29:28.188 --> 29:29.938
Narong transferred the land

294
29:30.855 --> 29:31.688
to Sak,

295
29:33.646 --> 29:34.980
Pannee's older brother,

296
29:35.063 --> 29:36.855
without any sale taking place.

297
29:36.938 --> 29:39.521
What I'm wondering now is this.

298
29:39.605 --> 29:41.230
The murders of Thongdee's son

299
29:41.313 --> 29:42.605
and Mued

300
29:43.896 --> 29:46.438
may have been committed by the same person.

301
29:47.480 --> 29:48.480
As for Sak's murder,

302
29:49.355 --> 29:51.271
I think someone else was responsible.

303
29:53.271 --> 29:55.855
As for the murders where the victims' teeth were missing,

304
29:57.063 --> 30:00.730
which resemble the Phii Pong cases in other provinces…

305
30:05.105 --> 30:06.688
I think whoever committed them

306
30:08.271 --> 30:11.230
has some kind of connection to this family.

307
30:55.105 --> 30:55.938
Nee?

308
31:01.771 --> 31:02.605
Nee.

309
31:08.771 --> 31:10.021
Why aren't you asleep?

310
31:13.355 --> 31:14.730
Is Sak coming back?

311
31:21.146 --> 31:21.980
Yeah.

312
31:38.813 --> 31:40.021
Tell him to go away.

313
31:41.605 --> 31:42.855
I already gave him so much.

314
31:44.313 --> 31:45.438
Wasn't that enough?

315
31:52.396 --> 31:53.730
We gave him the land.

316
31:57.480 --> 31:59.105
I don't know what else he wants.

317
32:07.480 --> 32:09.313
Let's stop, Pannee.

318
32:10.438 --> 32:11.688
I can't do this anymore.

319
32:46.230 --> 32:47.063
Come.

320
